# MAPS REGISTRY. Read at build time by bolt (ctf_maps, ctf_lobby).
# The number of a map (score "result map_vote", the vote) is its index in MAPS + 1.
# Every map works the same way; its functions ctf_maps:map/<id>/<event> are generated from its
# entry here (ctf_maps:gen). The world layout: registry/world.bolt.
# A point is [x, y, z], an area (fill) is [x1, y1, z1, x2, y2, z2].
#
#   name, vote_slot, map_item - the vote button in the lobby: name, hotbar slot, map_id of the map
#   title - JSON text shown at the match start
#   time - the map has its own daylight: the daylight cycle is on, the time is set at the start
#   music - disc, pitch, period (ticks: when it is played again); None - no music
#   template - the corner of the map template: it is cloned into the arena (ctf_maps:internal/prepare)
#   prepare_fills - fills of the arena right after the template marker (bug fixes)
#   entities - summoned at the clone: entity, point, NBT
#   win_trigger - the flag is delivered here
#   spawns - every freeze: each side is spread around [x, z], under y, with spread distance and range
#   wall_block - the block of the borders
#   walls - the borders, in order. Closed in freeze ("block" replaces "replaces", by default the
#           wall_block replaces air), opened in round:
#             open - "replace": only the wall block is removed (default), "all": the whole area,
#                    None: never opened
#             open_area - another area when it is opened
#             fx - the opening is shown: particles [particle, [dx, dy, dz], speed, count] at the point
#                  "at" and the sound at "sound_at" (by default "at")
#   areas, points - the named coordinates used above
#   loot - loot crate landing points (the block where a box lands)

def fx(at, particles, sound_at=None):
    if sound_at is None:
        sound_at = at
    return {"at": at, "particles": particles, "sound_at": sound_at}

